ose graphs which have torsion in cohomology H^{1,2v-3}_{A_3}(G) (e.g. loopless graphs which have a 3-cycle). ... Finally, we give examples of calculations of width of H^{1,*}_{A_3}(G) and of cohomology H^{1,(m-1)(v-2)+1}_{A_m}(G) for m>3.\\n# arXiv++ Combinatorics\\n\\nBrowse math.CO papers from arXiv\\n\\n## On the first group of the chromatic cohomology of graphs\\n\\nMilena D. Pabiniak, Jozef H. Przytycki, Radmila Sazdanovic\\n\\nPublished: 2006-07-13\\n\\nComments: 37 pages, 23 figures\\n\\nNote:\\n\\nDOI: 10.1007/s10711-008-9307-4\\n\\nchromatic polynomial cohomology graph group polynomial\\n\\n# • BIB • PDF • ARXIV •\\n\\n### Abstract\\n\\nThe algebra of truncated polynomials A_m=Z[x]/(x^m) plays an important role in the theory of Khovanov and Khovanov-Rozansky homology of links. We have demonstrated that Hochschild homology is closely related to Khovanov homology via comultiplication free graph cohomology. It is not difficult to compute Hochschild homology of A_m and the only torsion, equal to Z_m, appears in gradings (i,m(i+1)/2) for any positive odd i. We analyze here the grading of graph cohomology which is producing torsion for a polygon. We find completely the cohomology H^{1,v-1}_{A_2}(G) and H^{1,2v-3}_{A_3}(G). The group H^{1,v-1}_{A_2}(G) is closely related to the standard graph cohomology, except that the boundary of an edge is the sum of endpoints instead of the difference. The result about H^{1,v-1}_{A_2}(G) gives as a corollary a fact about Khovanov homology of alternating and + or - adequate link diagrams. The group H^{1,2v-3}_{A_3}(G) can be computed from the homology of a cell complex, X_{Δ,4}(G), built from the graph G. In particular, we prove that A_3 cohomology can have any torsion. We give a simple and complete characterization of those graphs which have torsion in cohomology H^{1,2v-3}_{A_3}(G) (e.g. loopless graphs which have a 3-cycle). We also construct graphs which have the same (di)chromatic polynomial but different H^{1,2v-3}_{A_3}(G). Finally, we give examples of calculations of width of H^{1,*}_{A_3}(G) and of cohomology H^{1,(m-1)(v-2)+1}_{A_m}(G) for m>3.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nOn the first group of the chromatic cohomology of graphs (https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0607326)\\nciteturn2academia15 [wordlim: 200] Published: 20.3 years ago; The group H^{1,2v-3}_{A_3}(G) can be computed from the homology of a cell complex, X_{\\\\Delta,4}(G), built from the graph G. ... We give a simple and complete characterization of those graphs which have torsion in cohomology H^{1,2v-3}_{A_3}(G) (e.g. loopless graphs which have a 3-cycle). ... Finally, we give examples of calculations of width of H^{1,*}_{A_3}(G) and of cohomology H^{1,(m-1)(v-2)+1}_{A_m}(G) for m>3.\\nTitle: On the first group of the chromatic cohomology of graphs\\nAuthors: Milena D. Pabiniak, Jozef H. Przytycki, Radmila Sazdanovic\\nDate: Thu Jul 13 21:52:01 2006\\n\\nThe algebra of truncated polynomials A_m=Z[x]/(x^m) plays an important role in the theory of Khovanov and Khovanov-Rozansky homology of links. We have demonstrated that Hochschild homology is closely related to Khovanov homology via comultiplication free graph cohomology. It is not difficult to compute Hochschild homology of A_m and the only torsion, equal to Z_m, appears in gradings (i,m(i+1)/2) for any positive odd i. We analyze here the grading of graph cohomology which is producing torsion for a polygon. We find completely the cohomology H^{1,v-1}_{A_2}(G) and H^{1,2v-3}_{A_3}(G). The group H^{1,v-1}_{A_2}(G) is closely related to the standard graph cohomology, except that the boundary of an edge is the sum of endpoints instead of the difference. The result about H^{1,v-1}_{A_2}(G) gives as a corollary a fact about Khovanov homology of alternating and + or - adequate link diagrams. The group H^{1,2v-3}_{A_3}(G) can be computed from the homology of a cell complex, X_{\\\\Delta,4}(G), built from the graph G. In particular, we prove that A_3 cohomology can have any torsion. We give a simple and complete characterization of those graphs which have torsion in cohomology H^{1,2v-3}_{A_3}(G) (e.g. loopless graphs which have a 3-cycle). We also construct graphs which have the same (di)chromatic polynomial but different H^{1,2v-3}_{A_3}(G). Finally, we give examples of calculations of width of H^{1,*}_{A_3}(G) and of cohomology H^{1,(m-1)(v-2)+1}_{A_m}(G) for m>3.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nLift theorems for representations of matroids over pastures... (https://arxivlens.com/paperview/details/lift-theorems-for-representations-of-matroids-over-pastures-8803-1862871)\\nciteturn2search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.3 years ago; Crawled: last month; We prove several lift theorems for representations of matroids over pastures, including a generalization of Pendavingh and van Zwam's Lift Theorem for partial fields. ... @article{baker2021lift, title = {Lift theorems for representations of matroids over pastures}, author = {Baker, Matthew and Lorscheid, Oliver}, year = {2021}, eprint = {2107.00981}, archivePrefix = {arXiv}, primaryClass = {math.CO}, }\\n\\nBack ArXiv math.CO Lift theorems for representations of matroids over pastures\\n\\nArXiv math.CO\\n\\n# Lift theorems for representations of matroids over pastures\\n\\nMatthew Baker, Oliver Lorscheid\\n\\n2107.00981 Published Jul 5, 2021\\n\\n### Publication\\n\\nPublished: Jul 05, 2021\\n\\nCategories: math.CO\\n\\n### Metrics\\n\\nSource: ArXiv\\n\\n### AI Quick Summary\\n\\nThis paper proves several lift theorems for matroid representations over pastures, generalizing previous results for partial fields. It establishes new insights, such as the idempotency of the lift construction, and applies these findings to unique lifting of hexagonal representations to near-regular representations.\\n\\n### Paper Preview\\n\\n### Abstract\\n\\nPastures are a class of field-like algebraic 